  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1401.18 Factor of safety",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1401.18 “Factor of safety” means the ratio of the actual load capacity of a carnival or amusement ride to the load capacity the carnival or amusement ride could tolerate, as established in the manufacturing process.\n\nSource. #4321, eff 10-6-87; ss by #4531, eff 1-1-89; ss by #5940, INTERIM, eff 1-1-95; ss by #5952, eff 1-24-95, EXPIRED: 1-24-03\n\nNew. #7833, INTERIM, eff 2-22-03, EXPIRED: 8-21-03\n\nNew. #8045, eff 2-20-04; ss by #8342, eff 4-28-05, EXPIRED: 1-2-14 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)\n\nNew. #10507, eff 1-21-14, EXPIRED: 1-21-24 (formerly Saf-C 1401.11)\n\nNew. #14011, INTERIM, eff 6-27-24; ss by #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (formerly Saf-C 1401.14)",
